  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Trade Republic x SheLeads. Round 2.

The first session was all about building wealth. This one focused on the career that funds it.
For that, early-career women joined us in Berlin last week.

Our Product Owner <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/in/aszaniawska?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Aleksandra S.</a>, Compliance Manager <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/in/juliane-kisse-a6bbb4232?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Juliane Kisse</a> and Corporate Development Associate <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/in/franziska-brandmann-601598138?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>Franziska Brandmann</a> took a deep dive into:

-- What ownership looks like when teams move fast.
-- How to build visibility while navigating a high-growth company. 
-- Where different functions cross paths and collaborate.

Followed by an open Q&amp;A over drinks and food.

Thanks to <a class="link" href="https://de.linkedin.com/company/she-leads-ev?trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>SheLeads</a> and everyone who came.

