  <div class="attributed-text-segment-list__container relative mt-1 mb-1.5 babybear:mt-0 babybear:mb-0.5">
    <p class="attributed-text-segment-list__content text-color-text !text-sm whitespace-pre-wrap break-words
        " dir="ltr" data-test-id="main-feed-activity-card__commentary">Tax wrappers are a great way to help people start investing.

Several European countries have already launched tax wrappers to make investing easier. From France's PEA to Poland's IKE.

Most European countries still do not have one, and progress is slow.

Meanwhile, the pension gap keeps growing. Young Europeans are paying into a system built on promises their generation may never fully see.

Tax wrappers will not close that gap themselves. But they are one of the clearest tools Europe has to get more people building wealth directly in the capital markets.

We think every European should have access to one.

Do you agree?

<a class="link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/signup/cold-join?session_redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.linkedin.com%2Ffeed%2Fhashtag%2Ftraderepublic&amp;_l=de&amp;trk=organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" target="_self" data-tracking-control-name="organization_guest_main-feed-card-text" data-tracking-will-navigate>#TradeRepublic</a>

Investing involves risks. Past performance is not a reliable indicator of future results. </p>
